  "lines": [
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "I asked AI for a book about our town. It gave me a title, an author, everything. But the book doesn't exist! What happened?",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "robot",
          "label": "SOUNDS SURE"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "warn",
          "label": "BUT FAKE?"
        },
        "subtitle": "Why AI makes things up"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "That's called a hallucination. Today: why it happens, where it shows up most, and how to catch it. Plus a quiz!",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "TODAY",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🤖",
            "label": "Why?",
            "cue": "why"
          },
          {
            "icon": "📍",
            "label": "Where",
            "cue": "where"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🔍",
            "label": "Catch it",
            "cue": "catch"
          },
          {
            "icon": "❓",
            "label": "Quiz",
            "cue": "quiz"
          }
        ]
      },
      "punch": "hallucination"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "A hallucination? Like seeing things?",
      "chapter": "What it is"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Sort of! In AI, it means the answer sounds confident and real, but it's false or made up.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "warn",
        "text": "Confident, but false",
        "cue": "confident",
        "sub": "Sounds real. Isn't.",
        "sub_cue": "false"
      },
      "punch": "false"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So it's lying to me?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Not on purpose. Lying means you know the truth and hide it. The AI isn't checking truth at all. It's making text that sounds right.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "LYING",
          "color": "#FF4D6D",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Knows truth, hides it",
              "icon": "🤥",
              "cue": "know",
              "tick": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "AI MISTAKE",
          "color": "#0A84FF",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Not checking truth",
              "icon": "robot",
              "cue": "checking",
              "tick": true
            },
            {
              "text": "Just sounds right",
              "icon": "chat",
              "cue": "sounds",
              "tick": true
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Then why does it make things up?",
      "chapter": "Why it happens"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Remember, it's a next-word predictor. It picks words that are likely to come next, based on patterns it learned. Likely isn't the same as true.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "brain",
        "text": "Likely ≠ true",
        "cue": "likely"
      },
      "punch": "true"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "But why invent a whole book?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Book titles have a pattern: a catchy title, an author name, a year. If it never saw the real answer, it can still fill in that pattern.",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "HOW A FAKE BOOK HAPPENS",
        "traveler": "📕",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "📖",
            "label": "Title",
            "cue": "titles"
          },
          {
            "icon": "👤",
            "label": "Author",
            "cue": "author"
          },
          {
            "icon": "📅",
            "label": "Year",
            "cue": "year"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🧩",
            "label": "Fills the gaps",
            "cue": "fill"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So it's guessing the shape of an answer."
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Exactly. And it's trained to be helpful, so it usually tries to answer instead of saying, I don't know.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🙋",
        "text": "Tries to help, even when unsure",
        "cue": "helpful"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Like a student bluffing on a test?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "A bit! Except it doesn't know it's bluffing. That's why it sounds so calm and sure.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "😐",
        "text": "Bluffing, without knowing it",
        "cue": "bluffing",
        "sub": "calm and sure",
        "sub_cue": "calm"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Can a question trick it?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Sometimes! If your question has a wrong idea built in, it might go along with it. Good tools often push back, but not always.",
      "board": {
        "type": "chat",
        "title": "A TRICK QUESTION",
        "color": "#FF8C42",
        "items": [
          {
            "who": "user",
            "text": "Why is the moon made of cheese?",
            "cue": "wrong"
          },
          {
            "who": "bot",
            "text": "It isn't! It's rock.",
            "cue": "push"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "What makes it more likely to happen?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Rare topics, very specific details, and anything after its training stopped. Less information means more guessing.",
      "board": {
        "type": "checklist",
        "title": "MORE LIKELY WITH",
        "icon": "warn",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Rare topics",
            "cue": "rare",
            "ok": false
          },
          {
            "text": "Very specific details",
            "cue": "specific",
            "ok": false
          },
          {
            "text": "Very recent events",
            "cue": "after",
            "ok": false
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So what should I watch out for most?",
      "chapter": "Danger zones"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Quotes, numbers, dates and sources. It can invent a quote nobody said, a statistic, or a link that goes nowhere.",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "WATCH OUT",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "💬",
            "label": "Quotes",
            "cue": "quotes"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🔢",
            "label": "Numbers",
            "cue": "numbers"
          },
          {
            "icon": "📅",
            "label": "Dates",
            "cue": "dates"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🔗",
            "label": "Sources",
            "cue": "sources"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#FF4D6D"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Fake links? Really?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Yes! A link can look perfect, with a real website name, and still lead nowhere. Always click and check.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🔗",
        "text": "Looks real ≠ is real",
        "cue": "look",
        "sub": "Click it. Check it.",
        "sub_cue": "click"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Has that caused real problems?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Yes. There have been news stories about people trusting made-up references, even in serious work. That's why checking matters.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "warn",
        "text": "Fake references, real trouble",
        "cue": "references"
      },
      "punch": "checking"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "What about health or money stuff?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "That's where mistakes hurt most. Use AI to understand the basics, but make decisions with a doctor or another real expert.",
