    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Okay, give me a game plan.",
      "chapter": "How to catch it"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Four habits. Ask for sources. Open them. Cross-check with a trusted site. And ask again in a different way.",
      "board": {
        "type": "cycle",
        "title": "FACT-CHECK LOOP",
        "center": "🔍",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "📚",
            "label": "Ask for sources",
            "cue": "sources"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🔗",
            "label": "Open them",
            "cue": "open"
          },
          {
            "icon": "✅",
            "label": "Cross-check",
            "cue": "cross"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🔁",
            "label": "Ask differently",
            "cue": "different"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#2ECC71"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Why ask again differently?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "If the answers keep changing, that's a warning sign. Real facts usually stay the same.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "warn",
        "text": "Answers keep changing? Warning!",
        "cue": "changing"
      },
      "punch": "warning"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Can't I just ask it how sure it is?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "You can, but its own confidence isn't reliable. It can say it's very sure and still be wrong. Checking beats trusting.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🎯",
        "text": "Checking beats trusting",
        "cue": "checking"
      },
      "punch": "checking"
    },
